:"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation for deterministic finding fb102c9f260dc5b3d: added a bounded `## Verification` section that maps each existing ticket verify command to its observable documentation, reuse-surface, or signing-lifecycle proof. Feature scope, exclusions, historical preservation, and documentation policy remain unchanged.","timestamp":1787422849135356001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan-review remediation for blocking finding f00ff634d754e9ac0 and surfaced findings fd2b03d2db1e45ec4/fde0e86925a5589df: replaced subjective prose-quality ACs with four explicit current-certificate facts and an explicit legacy non-certification rule; enumerated the seven operator-approved edit surfaces; preserved the test-pinned generic HMAC API text; and added a one-time search plus per-file evidence comment as the direct content oracle. This remains audit evidence, not mechanical writing enforcement, and the Markdown-only reduced test policy is unchanged.","timestamp":1787423495438339001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Final search classification\n\nThe required search returned 243 matches in 45 files.\n\n- Current operation-certificate guidance. `README.md`, `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md`, and `docs/sample-ticket-log.jsonl` are the approved edit set. Current gate statements now identify a DSSE envelope, an SSHSIG signature over its PAE bytes, an Ed25519 signing key, and the signing environment through the certificate principal. Legacy gate-HMAC statements say that the record remains readable but cannot certify a current gated operation. Generic HMAC API statements retain their non-gate meaning.\n- Accurate maintained material. `docs/cli-reference.md` contains generated current `verify-opcert` guidance. `docs/identity-setup.md` documents the separate authorship DSSE and SSHSIG flow. `docs/README.md` indexes the migration record. `docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md` cites DSSE as research grounding for literal-byte signing. These files need no F09 edit.\n- Mixed maintained material needing follow-up. `docs/attest-substrate.md` correctly describes DSSE and SSHSIG but still names the removed HMAC registry module and retired policy. `docs/exit-codes.md` still labels `verify-signature` as HMAC verification. `docs/config.md` still links to an HMAC snapshot trust model. `docs/identity.md` correctly documents authorship but uses stale HMAC comparisons for `verify-signature`. These paths and related public docstrings are recorded in `deft-intangible-xanclomys`. `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` correctly states that the webhook plugin provides no HMAC request signing, but its `mcp-hmac-signing-key` deployment path needs the read-only assessment recorded in `ultrashort-burnedout-gibbon`.\n- Historical decision and migration evidence. `docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md`, `docs/adr/README.md`, `docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md`, `docs/adr/0008-secrets-source-ssm.md`, `docs/adr/0009-review-bot-pipe.md`, `docs/adr/0014-inbound-webhook-auth.md`, `docs/adr/0043-operator-attested-completion-evidence.md`, `docs/adr/0044-asymmetric-attestation-substrate.md`, `docs/adr/0045-authenticated-identity.md`, `docs/adr/0046-security-posture-and-accepted-limitations.md`, `docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md`, `docs/adr/0073-reopen-invalidation-validity-on-read.md`, `docs/adr/0098-operation-scoped-config-and-provider-composition.md`, and `docs/adr/0101-non-codebase-acceptance-criterion-tag.md` record decisions at their historical points. They remain unchanged. Current guidance now cites ADR 0073 after its renumbering from the colliding ADR 0009 identifier.\n- Experiment evidence. All 15 matched paths under `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/`, including the criteria generator and run corpora, preserve captured inputs and outputs and remain unchanged.\n\n`docs/llm-framework.md` and `src/rebar/_cli/help/sign.txt` produced no keyword match and remain unchanged as required. The sign help accurately describes the generic command at its current level. Broader non-keyword signing language in the LLM guide is outside F09 and is recorded in `deft-intangible-xanclomys`.\n\n## Completed checks\n\n- The seven-file diff satisfies the four-fact current-certificate checklist and the explicit legacy non-certification checklist.\n- `git diff --name-only -- docs/llm-framework.md src/rebar/_cli/help/sign.txt` returned no paths.\n- Added prose passed a manual writing-policy review. No persistent prose or character check was added.\n- `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` passed.\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py -q` passed with 4 tests.\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_signature.py -q` passed with 23 tests.\n- The full suite was not run under the approved reduced policy.","timestamp":1787441918928218001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI evidence for Gerrit change 2133 patchset 1. GitHub run 32605850360 completed with failure. All four matrix environments reported one deterministic failure in tests/unit/test_snapshot_docs.py::test_hmac_trust_model_documented. The contract was introduced before ADR 0049 and still requires the legacy HMAC-SHA256 name, its lack of non-repudiation, and the current in-toto and DSSE shape. Investigation confirmed that ADR 0049 and the HMAC removal migration superseded HMAC for current operation certificates, while F09 retains accurate legacy compatibility guidance within docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md. The document now states that pre-migration gate records used HMAC-SHA256, that symmetric verification conferred forging power and no non-repudiation, and that these readable records return unknown_scheme and cannot certify a current gated operation. Focused verification passed. The snapshot documentation contract passed with 1 test, the reuse-surface contract passed with 4 tests, the signing lifecycle contract passed with 23 tests, the documentation index check passed, and git diff --check passed. The full suite was not run locally under the approved reduced policy.","timestamp":1787444192890587001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2133 patchset 2 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comments. It merged as aec961e9732b60a16a12213b83187857eec1a2ce, which is the current origin/main tip and retains the canonical F09 ticket trailer. GitHub run 32607511702 completed successfully from 2026-08-23T00:18:36Z through 2026-08-23T00:55:19Z, a duration of 2,203 seconds. This patchset followed the deterministic snapshot documentation contract failure on patchset 1. No CI retry was used. The focused local verification passed with 1 snapshot documentation test, 4 reuse-surface tests, 23 signing lifecycle tests, the documentation index check, and git diff --check. The full suite was not run locally under the approved reduced policy.","timestamp":1787446614608081001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"The first close attempt stopped at the unchecked acceptance-criteria precheck before invoking the completion verifier. During remediation, an unsafe shell quoting form interpreted Markdown backticks and temporarily expanded the description to 442,964 characters. No repository files changed. The description was restored through a literal single-quoted argument and then read back from the ticket store. The restored description is 3,793 characters, contains the Context, Plan, Verification, and Acceptance Criteria headings, has 10 checked acceptance items, and has no unchecked acceptance items. The acceptance wording is unchanged.","timestamp":1787446963958845001}],"created_at":1787417206852198001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"380ab159-6fab-4ff3-bdec-b11cbf5ab98b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"aa0e-c53c-e1ba-49c3"},{"link_uuid":"210b9251-31d4-4c1c-916f-608d7a0683c8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"eaa7-0cda-9fae-4131"}],"description":"## Context\nMaintained guidance conflates generic HMAC manifest signatures with current plan-review and completion-verifier operation certificates. ADR 0044 defines the DSSE and SSHSIG substrate. ADR 0049 defines asymmetric, environment-attributed operation certificates and legacy compatibility.\n\n## Plan\n- Use the existing file-impact set as the positive edit scope: `README.md`, `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md`, `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, and `docs/sample-ticket-log.jsonl`.\n- Classify each gate-adjacent signature statement in those files as current operation-certificate guidance, generic HMAC manifest/API guidance, legacy HMAC compatibility, or historical migration evidence.\n- Make every current plan-review or completion-verifier statement identify all four implemented facts: a DSSE envelope, SSHSIG signing, an Ed25519 key, and environment-attributed signer identity.\n- Make every legacy HMAC compatibility statement say that the record remains readable but cannot certify a current gated operation.\n- Preserve generic HMAC manifest-signing guidance for other consumers. In `docs/reuse-surface.md`, change only incorrect gate-consumer attribution while retaining the source-contract statements pinned by `tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py`, including the generic `sign_manifest` API and hex-HMAC `compute_signature` result.\n- Preserve ADR and migration history. Keep `src/rebar/_cli/help/sign.txt` and `docs/llm-framework.md` unchanged because their current statements are accurate.\n- Use a one-time repository search plus an auditable per-file classification comment to detect omissions. This is review evidence, not a persistent string gate or mechanical prose-quality policy.\n- Do not add mechanical writing enforcement. Do not change the Markdown-only reduced test policy.\n\n## Verification\n- Run `rg -n \"HMAC|DSSE|SSHSIG|operation[- ]certificate\" README.md docs src/rebar/_cli/help/sign.txt`, classify every gate-adjacent hit, and record the path plus classification in a ticket comment. Any hit outside the positive edit set must be recorded as accurate, historical, excluded, or follow-up scope before completion.\n- Review `git diff -- README.md docs/manifest-signing.md docs/event-schema.md docs/reuse-surface.md docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md docs/plan-review-gate.md docs/sample-ticket-log.jsonl` against the four-fact current-certificate checklist and the explicit non-certifying legacy-HMAC checklist. Record the completed checklist in the ticket comment rather than adding an automated wording gate.\n- Run `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` to prove documentation links and index entries remain valid.\n- Run `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py -q` to prove reusable generic-HMAC API documentation still matches the source contract.\n- Run `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_signature.py -q` to prove current and legacy signing lifecycle contracts remain green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every changed current-gate statement identifies DSSE, SSHSIG, Ed25519, and environment attribution.\n- [x] Every changed legacy-HMAC statement explicitly says it cannot certify current gated operations.\n- [x] Generic HMAC manifest/API statements retain their implemented non-gate meaning.\n- [x] A ticket comment classifies every gate-adjacent search hit by path and consumer role.\n- [x] ADR and migration history remains intact.\n- [x] `src/rebar/_cli/help/sign.txt` remains unchanged.\n- [x] `docs/llm-framework.md` remains unchanged.\n- [x] All commands in `## Verification` pass or produce the recorded classification evidence.\n- [x] No persistent mechanical writing-enforcement check is introduced.\n- [x] The Markdown-only reduced test policy remains unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"README.md","reason":"Correct operation-certificate summary claims."},{"path":"docs/manifest-signing.md","reason":"Separate generic HMAC manifest signing from current gate certificates."},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"Describe current and legacy signature record roles."},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"Correct reusable signing and gate-consumer guidance."},{"path":"docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md","reason":"Correct the current gate trust model."},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"Correct plan-review and completion certificate guidance."},{"path":"docs/sample-ticket-log.jsonl","reason":"Keep the maintained signature example aligned with its documented mechanism."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f7e4-4d33-f231-4774"],["relates_to","aa0e-c53c-e1ba-49c3"],["relates_to","eaa7-0cda-9fae-4131"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f7e4-4d33-f231-4774","parent_status_uuid":"7785425f-b2dc-45b0-b0d1-62d70835fb40","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["documentation","f09","security"],"ticket_id":"89af-b080-1216-4229","ticket_type":"story","title":"F09 align operation-certificate guidance with asymmetric signing","verify_commands":[{"command":"python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Documentation links and index remain valid"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_reuse_surface_doc.py -q","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"Reusable signing API documentation matches source"},{"command":"python -